<section class="tool-area">
  <div class="tool-container">
    <fieldset class="form-fieldset">
      <legend>Basic Meta Tags</legend>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="mt-title">Page Title *</label>
        <input type="text" id="mt-title" placeholder="My Page Title (50-60 characters)">
        <p class="form-hint"><span id="mt-title-count">0</span>/60 characters</p>
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="mt-description">Meta Description *</label>
        <textarea id="mt-description" rows="2" placeholder="A compelling description of your page (120-155 characters)"></textarea>
        <p class="form-hint"><span id="mt-desc-count">0</span>/155 characters</p>
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="mt-keywords">Keywords (optional)</label>
        <input type="text" id="mt-keywords" placeholder="seo, meta tags, generator">
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="mt-robots">Robots</label>
        <select id="mt-robots">
          <option value="index, follow">Index, Follow (default)</option>
          <option value="index, nofollow">Index, NoFollow</option>
          <option value="noindex, follow">NoIndex, Follow</option>
          <option value="noindex, nofollow">NoIndex, NoFollow</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="mt-canonical">Canonical URL</label>
        <input type="url" id="mt-canonical" placeholder="https://example.com/page">
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="mt-locale">Language / Locale</label>
        <input type="text" id="mt-locale" value="en_US" placeholder="en_US">
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="form-fieldset">
      <legend>Open Graph (Facebook, LinkedIn, etc.)</legend>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="mt-og-title">OG Title</label>
        <input type="text" id="mt-og-title" placeholder="Auto-filled from Page Title">
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="mt-og-desc">OG Description</label>
        <textarea id="mt-og-desc" rows="2" placeholder="Auto-filled from Meta Description"></textarea>
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="mt-og-image">OG Image URL</label>
        <input type="url" id="mt-og-image" placeholder="https://example.com/image.jpg">
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="mt-og-type">OG Type</label>
        <select id="mt-og-type">
          <option value="website">Website</option>
          <option value="article">Article</option>
          <option value="product">Product</option>
          <option value="profile">Profile</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="mt-og-site">Site Name</label>
        <input type="text" id="mt-og-site" placeholder="My Website">
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="form-fieldset">
      <legend>Twitter Card</legend>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="mt-tw-card">Card Type</label>
        <select id="mt-tw-card">
          <option value="summary_large_image">Summary Large Image</option>
          <option value="summary">Summary</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="mt-tw-title">Twitter Title</label>
        <input type="text" id="mt-tw-title" placeholder="Auto-filled from Page Title">
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="mt-tw-desc">Twitter Description</label>
        <textarea id="mt-tw-desc" rows="2" placeholder="Auto-filled from Meta Description"></textarea>
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="mt-tw-image">Twitter Image URL</label>
        <input type="url" id="mt-tw-image" placeholder="https://example.com/image.jpg">
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="mt-tw-site">Twitter @Handle</label>
        <input type="text" id="mt-tw-site" placeholder="@yourhandle">
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <div class="tool-actions">
      <button class="btn-primary" onclick="generateMetaTags()">Generate Meta Tags</button>
      <button class="btn-secondary" onclick="copyMetaTags()">Copy to Clipboard</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="tool-output" id="meta-result">
    <h3>Generated Meta Tags</h3>
    <pre><code id="meta-output">Fill in the fields above and click Generate...</code></pre>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="faq">
  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <details>
    <summary>What is the ideal length for a meta title tag?</summary>
    <p>Google typically displays up to 60 characters (about 580 pixels). Keep your title between 50-60 characters for optimal display. The most important keywords should appear at the beginning.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>What is the ideal length for a meta description?</summary>
    <p>Google displays up to about 155 characters (roughly 920 pixels). Aim for 120-155 characters. While meta descriptions don't directly affect rankings, they significantly impact click-through rates.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>What are Open Graph tags and why do I need them?</summary>
    <p>Open Graph tags control how your content appears when shared on Facebook, LinkedIn, and other social platforms. They set the title, description, image, and type of the shared link preview.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>Where do I put these meta tags?</summary>
    <p>All meta tags go inside the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> section of your HTML document. If you use a CMS like WordPress, you can add them via plugins like Yoast SEO or Rank Math, or directly in your theme's header.php.</p>
  </details>
</section>
